WEBVTT

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:09.900
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Thursday the twenty-first. Can you all hear me, or am I doing the Teams mime again?</v>

00:00:10.529 --> 00:00:15.779
<v Grace Liu>Yeah, you're fine. Sorry, only just sat down. Traffic on the ring road was ridiculous.</v>

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:22.190
<v Marcus Hale>Same queue, probably. Plenty of time to admire the back of a bus.</v>

00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:32.420
<v Tomasz Nowak>At least your bus probably wasn't as hot as the portakabin. The heating in there, honestly. Tropical. Just moaning, before anyone puts my name against it.</v>

00:00:34.149 --> 00:00:38.000
<v Hannah Price>There's a birthday cake in the office, if that improves matters.</v>

00:00:39.950 --> 00:00:42.750
<v Aisha Begum>Depends whether it's survived being in that heat.</v>

00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:47.549
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, before this becomes the cake meeting. Couple of closed bits first.</v>

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:55.170
<v Sarah Okafor>Already swapped the filter on the palletiser yesterday. That's done, not another job for today.</v>

00:00:56.530 --> 00:01:00.380
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yep, that's the one I thought was still showing. Done, understood.</v>

00:01:00.929 --> 00:01:07.579
<v Sarah Okafor>And tested the Line 1 Hydraulic Power Unit yesterday and it's all fine now. That one's closed as well.</v>

00:01:09.329 --> 00:01:12.129
<v Aisha Begum>Lovely. No outstanding bit hanging off that, then.</v>

00:01:12.659 --> 00:01:17.909
<v Hannah Price>Quality side, finished the repair on the CT1 last night. Nothing left on that repair.</v>

00:01:18.650 --> 00:01:20.049
<v Sarah Okafor>Good, another closed one.</v>

00:01:21.739 --> 00:01:31.189
<v Aisha Begum>Um, just an observation from nights: noticed the GT1 Fuel Gas Valve was running a bit warm, but it settled down. Not raising a job off that.</v>

00:01:32.420 --> 00:01:35.219
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, so, settled rather than still climbing. Understood.</v>

00:01:35.549 --> 00:01:43.950
<v Hannah Price>Similar sort of thing, I heard a slight rattle from the Injection Moulding Line 1. Nothing to action yet, just mentioning what I heard.</v>

00:01:46.319 --> 00:01:49.819
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay. Both observations, neither going down as a new action.</v>

00:01:50.349 --> 00:01:56.650
<v Marcus Hale>And the other one hasn't moved: can't get to the compressor one until production gives us a window.</v>

00:01:58.209 --> 00:02:03.109
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah, there's no window available on the schedule. Still blocked, not a booked job.</v>

00:02:05.209 --> 00:02:09.759
<v Sarah Okafor>Right. We're not agreeing to get that done today when there's no access.</v>

00:02:11.060 --> 00:02:21.909
<v Fiona Doyle>On what I can take, I'll replace the seals on the GT2 water valve by end of day. Not an emergency but don't let it slip, that's how I'm treating it.</v>

00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:29.009
<v Tomasz Nowak>Just the seals on the GT2 water valve, yeah? Not changing the whole valve?</v>

00:02:30.689 --> 00:02:36.289
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah, just the seals. I'll do the replacement, not just stick it on somebody else's list.</v>

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:43.289
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Fiona. Yours, by end of day. Not an emergency, but it does need to stay on track.</v>

00:02:44.699 --> 00:02:45.900
<v Fiona Doyle>Yep, agreed.</v>

00:02:46.210 --> 00:02:53.210
<v Sarah Okafor>And Fiona Doyle, can you chase the purchase order for the HV board tomorrow, if you've got a spare minute?</v>

00:02:53.900 --> 00:02:59.849
<v Fiona Doyle>Yes, I'll chase the purchase order for the HV board tomorrow, if I've got a spare minute.</v>

00:03:01.870 --> 00:03:06.069
<v Sarah Okafor>Cheers. Definitely the spare-minute one, not something to bump the seals for.</v>

00:03:07.509 --> 00:03:08.909
<v Fiona Doyle>Got you. Different urgency.</v>

00:03:09.789 --> 00:03:15.389
<v Sarah Okafor>Grace Liu, can you take vibration readings on the Water Booster Pump by Wednesday? It's urgent.</v>

00:03:17.110 --> 00:03:22.710
<v Grace Liu>Sorry, no, I can't take that. I haven't got the capacity to commit to the readings.</v>

00:03:24.060 --> 00:03:32.460
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, thanks for being straight. Marcus, can I hand that to you instead? Vibration readings on the Water Booster Pump, by Wednesday. It's urgent.</v>

00:03:33.409 --> 00:03:41.810
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, I'll take it from Grace Liu. I'll take vibration readings on the Water Booster Pump by Wednesday, and I've got that it's urgent.</v>

00:03:42.110 --> 00:03:47.360
<v Aisha Begum>Sorry, talking over you—readings only on that one, we're not agreeing an overhaul or anything?</v>

00:03:49.360 --> 00:03:51.810
<v Marcus Hale>Readings only, yeah. That's what I'm taking.</v>

00:03:52.169 --> 00:03:54.620
<v Sarah Okafor>Exactly. Keep the scope as it is.</v>

00:03:55.039 --> 00:04:01.689
<v Marcus Hale>While I'm on, I'll run a function test on the guard switch on two tomorrow. Low priority, that one.</v>

00:04:03.979 --> 00:04:09.580
<v Grace Liu>That's the routine function test, isn't it? Not saying we've got a failed guard in use?</v>

00:04:10.090 --> 00:04:13.240
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, routine function test. I'm not reporting a failure.</v>

00:04:15.569 --> 00:04:20.120
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, Marc, the guard switch on two is yours for tomorrow, low priority.</v>

00:04:21.819 --> 00:04:23.019
<v Marcus Hale>Yep, agreed.</v>

00:04:23.970 --> 00:04:30.970
<v Sarah Okafor>We've also got to do the pre-use checks on the forklifts by Wednesday. Fairly important. Anyone able to take that?</v>

00:04:31.399 --> 00:04:36.300
<v Grace Liu>It does need someone against it. I'm not volunteering, though; I can't take it.</v>

00:04:38.750 --> 00:04:43.300
<v Sarah Okafor>Anyone else for the forklifts? Don't want to mistake silence for a yes.</v>

00:04:44.589 --> 00:04:47.389
<v Tomasz Nowak>Not me, sorry. Can't commit to those checks.</v>

00:04:48.759 --> 00:04:50.860
<v Fiona Doyle>I can't add that one either.</v>

00:04:52.540 --> 00:04:58.839
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, pre-use checks on the forklifts remain unallocated. Still needed by Wednesday, fairly important, but nobody's taken them.</v>

00:05:01.319 --> 00:05:09.370
<v Aisha Begum>There's also grease and check the bearings on the CV01. Next Tuesday, normal priority. Needs doing, but I'm raising it, not taking it.</v>

00:05:11.160 --> 00:05:13.259
<v Sarah Okafor>Any takers for the CV01 bearings?</v>

00:05:14.959 --> 00:05:17.410
<v Marcus Hale>No room for that on mine, sorry.</v>

00:05:18.740 --> 00:05:24.339
<v Tomasz Nowak>Nor mine. I know it sounds like my sort of job, but I can't accept it.</v>

00:05:26.360 --> 00:05:32.310
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay. Grease and check the bearings on the CV01 stays without an owner. Next Tuesday, normal priority.</v>

00:05:33.360 --> 00:05:37.209
<v Hannah Price>That's clear. A couple of gaps, rather than pretending everything's covered.</v>

00:05:39.589 --> 00:05:50.439
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep. And just keeping the two priorities separate, Marcus has the urgent Water Booster Pump readings; Marc has the low-priority guard switch on two test. Same person, before Teams gets confused.</v>

00:05:52.899 --> 00:05:57.100
<v Marcus Hale>Both me, unfortunately for me. Pump by Wednesday, guard test tomorrow. Agreed.</v>

00:05:59.259 --> 00:06:09.060
<v Fiona Doyle>And mine's seals on the GT2 water valve by end of day, then the purchase order for the HV board tomorrow if I've got a spare minute. Clear.</v>

00:06:10.790 --> 00:06:16.389
<v Sarah Okafor>Good. Nobody against the forklifts or the CV01. Those are gaps, not quiet assignments to anyone.</v>

00:06:18.339 --> 00:06:20.790
<v Grace Liu>Yes, that's the distinction. No assumed volunteers.</v>

00:06:21.449 --> 00:06:25.300
<v Hannah Price>Much less ambiguity over who's interested in the cake, I suspect.</v>

00:06:25.930 --> 00:06:27.680
<v Tomasz Nowak>Normal priority. Unless it's chocolate.</v>

00:06:28.019 --> 00:06:32.220
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, that's us. No more jobs hidden in the banter. Thanks, everyone.</v>

00:06:33.560 --> 00:06:34.759
<v Marcus Hale>Cheers, all.</v>
